  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\nfrac{{{{[ {( {34.45} )} ]}²} - {{( {11.75} )}²}] × 5.15}}{{[ {{{( {25.75} )}²} + ( {25.75 × 20.45} )} ] × 22.7}}\n\n**Solution:**\n\nWe use the identity a² - b² = (a - b)(a + b):\n\n(34.45)² - (11.75)² = (34.45 - 11.75)(34.45 + 11.75) = 22.7 × 46.2\n\nNumerator : 22.7 × 46.2 × 5.15\n\nSimplify the denominator:\n\n⇒ [(25.75)² + (25.75×20.45)] × 22.7\n\n⇒ [(25.75 (25.75 + 20.45)] × 22.7\n\n⇒ 25.75 times 46.2 × 22.7\n\nCombine numerator and denominator and Divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n(22.7 × 46.2 × 5.15)/(25.75 times 46.2 × 22.7)\n\n⇒ (5.15)/(25.75) = (1)/(5)\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option 3.**\n\n134:T953",
